WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:08.341
A fraud check looks up the merchant on every card payment, 100,000 times a second.

2
00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:11.093
The database answers in 10 milliseconds.

3
00:00:11.093 --> 00:00:15.840
Redis, a cache in memory one hop away, answers in half a millisecond.

4
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.216
But Redis holds only some merchants.

5
00:00:18.216 --> 00:00:20.924
If it has the one you ask for, that's a hit.

6
00:00:20.924 --> 00:00:24.617
If not, it's a miss, and the lookup goes on to the database.

7
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:31.399
So the average lookup costs the hit ratio times half a millisecond, plus the miss ratio times 10.

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:37.829
At 90% hits, the hits add 0.45 milliseconds, and the misses add a whole millisecond.

9
00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:42.131
One lookup in ten costs more than the other nine together.

10
00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:46.777
And every miss is a query, so the database gets 10,000 a second.

11
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:47.663
Now 99%.

12
00:00:47.663 --> 00:00:58.512
It looks like nine points more, but it's ten times fewer misses: 1,000 queries a second, and the average falls to 0.6 milliseconds.

13
00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:05.265
At 99.9%, the average barely moves: it's already close to Redis's own half millisecond.

14
00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:08.434
But the database load drops tenfold again.

15
00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:10.773
So judge a cache by its misses.

16
00:01:10.967 --> 00:01:13.191
How does a small cache reach 99%?

17
00:01:13.191 --> 00:01:20.537
If all million merchants were equally popular, a cache holding a tenth of them would hit a tenth of the time.

18
00:01:20.733 --> 00:01:22.543
But real traffic is skewed.

19
00:01:22.543 --> 00:01:26.096
A supermarket chain pays thousands of times a minute.

20
00:01:26.096 --> 00:01:28.241
A bike repair shop, twice a day.

21
00:01:28.433 --> 00:01:36.191
With a common amount of skew, the top 1,000 merchants, a tenth of a percent, get half of all lookups.

22
00:01:36.191 --> 00:01:37.727
The top 10% get 84%.

23
00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:41.394
A small cache works because a few keys are hot.

24
00:01:41.394 --> 00:01:46.745
Then count its misses: from 90 to 99% hits, the slow trips fall tenfold.
